{
  name: "soc_dbg_ctrl"
  // TODO: remove the common testplans if not applicable
  import_testplans: ["hw/dv/tools/dvsim/testplans/csr_testplan.hjson",
                     "hw/dv/tools/dvsim/testplans/intr_test_testplan.hjson",
                     "hw/dv/tools/dvsim/testplans/tl_device_access_types_testplan.hjson"]
  testpoints: [
    {
      name: smoke
      desc: '''
            Smoke test accessing a major datapath within the soc_dbg_ctrl.

            **Stimulus**:
            - TBD

            **Checks**:
            - TBD
            '''
      stage: V1
      tests: ["soc_dbg_ctrl_smoke"]
    }
    {
      name: feature1
      desc: '''Add more test entries here like above.'''
      stage: V1
      tests: []
    }
    {
      name: trace_regs
      desc: '''
            Verify the registers that hardware updates after reset, which the generic CSR tests
            exclude: TRACE_DEBUG_POLICY_CATEGORY and TRACE_DEBUG_POLICY_VALID_RELOCKED on the core
            interface, and JTAG_TRACE_DEBUG_POLICY_CATEGORY, JTAG_TRACE_DEBUG_POLICY_VALID_RELOCKED,
            JTAG_BOOT_STATUS and JTAG_TRACE_SOC_DBG_STATE on the JTAG interface.

            **Stimulus**:
            - Randomize soc_dbg_state_i (Blank, PreProd, Prod, invalid), lc_dft_en_i,
              lc_hw_debug_en_i, lc_cpu_en_i and lc_rma_state_i (On, Off, invalid encodings)
              and boot_status_i.
            - In SocDbgStProd with lc_rma_state_i Off and lc_cpu_en_i On, program
              DEBUG_POLICY_CATEGORY_SHADOWED, DEBUG_POLICY_RELOCKED and
              DEBUG_POLICY_VALID_SHADOWED.
            - Walk the halt FSM through boot_status_i.lc_done, lc_raw_test_rma_i, lc_dft_en_i,
              halt_cpu_boot_i and JTAG_CONTROL.boot_continue.
            - After each change, read each register above through the interface it belongs to.

            **Checks**:
            - The four trace registers match the debug policy driven on soc_dbg_policy_bus_o and
              the policy predicted from the inputs.
            - While lc_dft_en_i is On, JTAG_BOOT_STATUS reflects boot_status_i (its lc_tx and MuBi
              fields through their strict true tests) and the halt FSM state, and
              JTAG_TRACE_SOC_DBG_STATE reflects soc_dbg_state_i; otherwise both read zero.
            '''
      stage: V2
      tests: []
    }
  ]

  covergroups: [
    {
      name: soc_dbg_ctrl_feature_cg
      desc: '''Describe the functionality covered by this covergroup.'''
    }
  ]
}
